WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.550
Checking the samples offline shows
what they do well, and the pipeline

2
00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:08.663
keeps all of it: the same sign-in,
the same secrets, the single grant.

3
00:00:08.663 --> 00:00:10.952
What they leave out starts with timing:

4
00:00:10.952 --> 00:00:15.175
they run when someone pushes a commit,
and drift doesn't wait for a commit.

5
00:00:15.175 --> 00:00:18.447
Their actions are referenced
by tags that can be moved,

6
00:00:18.447 --> 00:00:23.100
and an older major version at that, so
the pipeline pins each action to a commit.

7
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.558
Tool versions say latest,

8
00:00:24.558 --> 00:00:28.238
so the tool that produced the
evidence could change unreviewed.

9
00:00:28.238 --> 00:00:32.540
And the US Government sample,
copied as is, doesn't even parse.
